# F-Droid index metadata for com.hrbons.wordguesser.
# Sourced by ../rebuild-index.sh — plain shell assignments, no jq needed.
# Everything else in the index (version, size, hash, signer, SDK levels, permissions)
# is read from the APK itself, so only human-written fields live here.
#
# LICENSE was "MIT" until 2026-07-29 and is now "Proprietary", matching the other three. The user
# overruled the exception: abons/wordguesser-src is private again, the MIT LICENSE file is gone,
# and the official-F-Droid route (which is what the public source and the licence were for) is
# closed — see ../../fdroid-official/NOTES.md. The reasoning is the same one in the sister files:
# the apps are meant to earn, and MIT hands everyone the right to rebuild this and ship it.
# ⚠️ This retracts nothing already granted: v2.3 and earlier were published under MIT and whoever
# holds those bytes keeps that licence — the index says Proprietary for those entries anyway, which
# is the one inaccuracy here and was accepted knowingly.
#
# The plan was to let the live index keep saying MIT until the next release. That changed on
# 2026-07-29: SUMMARY/DESCRIPTION had to lose the "Wordle-style" wording (a trademark of another
# game), and this file is what feeds the index, so the rebuild happened there and then and carried
# the licence flip with it. The index no longer lags this file.
NAME="Word Guesser"
SUMMARY="Tiny native word-guessing game"
DESCRIPTION="A tiny, native Android word-guessing game in pure Kotlin — 17 languages, word length 4-8, daily puzzle, duels."
LICENSE="Proprietary"
CATEGORIES='["Games"]'
